      "message": "Actually, you can also have a const table mapping all led states to the led on/off conditions:\n\n#define LED_ON 1\n#define LED_OFF 0\n\nstatic const struct {\n    char led1:1;\n    char led2:1;\n    char pwr:1;\n} led_state_table[] \u003d {\n    [LED_STATE_CHARGE] \u003d {\n          .led1 \u003d LED_OFF, .led2 \u003d LED_ON, .pwr \u003d LED_OFF,\n    }\n    ...\n}\n\nAnd then have a function:\nconfig_led_state(enum led_state state)\n{\n    gpio_set_level(GPIO_CHG_LED1, led_state_table[state].led1);\n    gpio_set_level(GPIO_CHG_LED2, led_state_table[state].led2);\n    gpio_set_level(GPIO_PWR_LED, led_state_table[state].pwr);\n}\n\nThoughts?",
